# miyagi app: rules for Cursor agents

miyagi is a desktop overlay that turns any tutorial into a hands-on lesson whose steps are checked automatically. Several agents (Cursor and Claude Code) work in this repo in parallel, so these rules match `app/CLAUDE.md`. Read it, `app/README.md` and `shared/contracts/events.ts` before changing code.

## Lanes
- `app/` is Adrian's (Electron overlay: React, TypeScript, zustand). Edit only here.
- `server/` and `cli/` are Michael's (Python engine). `shared/contracts/` is Michael's too and changes only in a PR titled `contract: ...`, adding fields only, never renaming or removing one.
- Core files (`core/`, `bridge.ts`, `main.tsx`, `src/main/index.ts|engine.ts|platform.ts|context.ts`, `src/preload/`, `src/common/`, `package.json`, configs) belong to the integrator. Work inside a feature folder: `src/renderer/src/features/<feature>/` and `src/main/features/<feature>.ts`.

## Contract
- App and engine talk only through the WebSocket messages in `shared/contracts/events.ts`, `{type, payload}` both ways.
- The app builds against the mock in `app/mock/`; the engine emits the same events.
- Never hardcode lesson-specific names (metric names, 'loss', 'PINN'). Labels come from the data.

## Brand (anything visible)
- Read `app/brand/BRAND.md` first. Use `core/theme.ts` tokens only, no new hard-coded colors.
- Green only means passed. Off track has no hue: a white ring and "Not yet". Pastels only for options.
- No gradients, glows, neon, emoji or sparkles; the bonsai `MiyagiMark` replaces sparkle icons.
- The brand is lowercase: "miyagi". Copy is short, 12 words or fewer per card.
- Every surface grows out of the notch island and returns to it.

## Before you commit
- `npm run typecheck` in `app/` must pass.
- One branch per agent session, `adrian/<area>`. PR into `adrian/shell`; a human merges.
- No commits after Sun 15 Nov 12:00 PM Pacific.

## Secrets
- API keys live only in the settings feature (main process, safeStorage) or a local `.env`. Never commit, log or print a key.
